{%- comment -%}
  snippets/ci-footer.liquid
  Shared site footer. Included on every page with {% render 'ci-footer' %}.
  Single source of truth so the company line and links stay identical
  everywhere — edit here once, every page updates.
{%- endcomment -%}
<footer class="ci-footer" role="contentinfo">
  <div class="ci-footer__inner">
    <div class="tricolore-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p class="ci-footer__line">Crema Italia, LLC &middot; Lutz, Florida, USA &middot; cremaitalia.com</p>
    <ul class="ci-footer__links">
      <li><a href="mailto:info@cremaitalia.com">Contact</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://instagram.com/cremaitaliaco" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@cremaitaliaco</a></li>
    </ul>
    {%- comment -%}
      Policy links, added 2026-08-22. Four policies were published that day and this footer linked
      only Privacy - so the other three were reachable on the real domain by typing the URL and by
      no other route. Shopify links all of them from the CHECKOUT footer automatically, but nobody
      reaches checkout from a coming-soon page.

      Two deliberate choices, both matching what the POC storefront footer does:
        - They sit in their OWN quieter row rather than joining Contact and Instagram. These are
          fine print; those two are things a visitor might actually want.
        - Contact information is included even though Shopify marks it a "policy": it carries the
          legal name and physical address, which is the merchant-identity disclosure a visitor
          handing over an email address has most reason to want.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <ul class="ci-footer__links ci-footer__legal">
      <li><a href="/policies/privacy-policy">Privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/policies/terms-of-service">Terms</a></li>
      <li><a href="/policies/shipping-policy">Shipping</a></li>
      <li><a href="/policies/refund-policy">Returns</a></li>
      <li><a href="/policies/contact-information">Contact information</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</footer>
